# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file requests a review from the listed owners when a pull request
# touches the matching paths. It is *advisory*: GitHub only asks for the
# review, it does not block the merge. To make it binding, the repository
# needs a branch protection rule on `main` that requires review from a code
# owner ("Require review from Code Owners"). See docs/security.md for the
# exact settings to enable.
#
# Only `@Ayinkx` is listed. This organisation has no teams, and `@Ayinkx` is
# the only account with push or admin access to the repository, so it is the
# only account that can meaningfully act on a code-owner review request.
#
# There is deliberately no `* @Ayinkx` line. A global entry would route every
# pull request from the ~30 external contributors through a single person,
# which trains everyone to ignore review requests. The paths below are the
# ones where a change can silently widen the trust boundary of the repository,
# so those are the ones that deserve an owner.
#
# Later patterns win over earlier ones, so the most specific rules are listed
# last.

# --- Continuous integration and the actions trust boundary --------------
/.github/                    @Ayinkx
/.github/workflows/          @Ayinkx
/.github/dependabot.yml      @Ayinkx
/.github/CODEOWNERS          @Ayinkx

# --- The supply-chain guard and its test -------------------------------
/scripts/check_assets.py     @Ayinkx
/tests/test_asset_guard.py   @Ayinkx

# --- Dependency manifests ----------------------------------------------
/requirements.txt            @Ayinkx
/requirements-dev.txt        @Ayinkx
/package.json                @Ayinkx
/package-lock.json           @Ayinkx

# --- Build and packaging -----------------------------------------------
/Dockerfile                  @Ayinkx
/docker-compose.yml          @Ayinkx
/.dockerignore               @Ayinkx

# --- Files that execute on a contributor's machine ----------------------
# A `.vscode` task or a font-shaped file is exactly how the payload that was
# previously shipped in this repository was delivered.
/.vscode/                    @Ayinkx
/public/fonts/               @Ayinkx

# --- Ignore rules and security policy ----------------------------------
/.gitignore                  @Ayinkx
/SECURITY.md                 @Ayinkx
/docs/security.md            @Ayinkx
/CONTRIBUTING.md             @Ayinkx
